{"name":"Sedona Sage","hex":"#686d6c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sage","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Wise.","Grave; serious; solemn."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very wise person or spiritual teacher; someone of gravity and wisdom, especially, a teacher venerable for years, and of sound judgment and prudence; a grave or stoic philosopher."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sage"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sedona, Arizona","blocks":[{"text":"Sedona is a city straddling the county line between Coconino and Yavapai counties in the northern Verde Valley region of Arizona, United States. As of the 2020 census, Sedona had a population of 9,684. The city is within the Coconino National Forest."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Cathedral_Rock_-_Sedona_AZ-1.jpg/330px-Cathedral_Rock_-_Sedona_AZ-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sedona%2C_Arizona"},{"title":"Sage (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Sage is a grey-green resembling that of dried sage leaves. As a quaternary color, it is an equal mix of the tertiary colors citron and slate. The hex RGB color value of the adjacent sage swatch is BCB88A. For decades, some military flight jackets were made in sage green."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Sage_iPhone_17.jpg/330px-Sage_iPhone_17.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sage_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Us-az-sd%29.gif/120px-Us-az-sd%29.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Us-az-sd%29.gif/250px-Us-az-sd%29.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb